WEBVTT

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.400
My long summer vacation has come to an end.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.150
Hello.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.150
Oh, Natsuki.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.610
It's been such a long time.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.870
Oh... yeah, it's been a while.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.160
Karin, is there something different about you?

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.370
I don't <i>think</i> so!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.630
That's right.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.040
Everything's as it's always been.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.960
Exactly!

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.010
Kabuki Seal!

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.130
I-Is this...

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.010
your second term debut?

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.810
So that's the dream I had.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.480
A second term debut?

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.030
Is that like your debut into high society?

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.490
No, it wasn't like that...

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.360
To put it simply,

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.530
it was more like a change of image to
celebrate the end of summer vacation.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.660
My fingernails have done a second term debut.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.580
Oh, you got a manicure!

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.580
Wow, they're all sparkly!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.750
Would you like to try it, Botan-senpai?

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.800
I'll give you one, too.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.590
Your feminine appeal is sky high as always, Karin!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.850
D-Don't get the wrong idea.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.520
It's not like I bought this with you in mind!

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.110
Uh, what was that all about?

00:02:59.450 --> 00:02:59.990
Tsun...

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.610
...dere!

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.530
What's that?

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.870
Are you goofing around?

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.870
Okay, let's rip off her fingernails.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.830
I'm sorry! I got carried away!

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.620
For such close friends, they sure are merciless.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.800
It's just that, since we were discussing image changes,

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.960
I thought I might try one, too.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.260
So why did you go for that one?

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.600
Well, you see, I have these pigtails, right?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.100
I think most people totally
associate pigtails with tsundere!

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:28.720
Totally!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.770
You changed your personality
to match your appearance?!

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:36.400
Well, a person's appearance and
their personality do tend to match.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.360
They say, "Don't judge a book by its cover,"

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:43.360
but a person's personality does show
in their appearance surprisingly often.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.160
It irks me to hear that coming from her.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.700
If there's a fat guy in a band,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:47.990
Yeah!

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:48.990
you can bet he's the drummer.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.580
If you see a delinquent
with a pompadour nowadays,

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.870
The hell are you lookin' at?!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.920
you can bet he's from Saitama Prefecture.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.420
That's just prejudice!

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.210
Why do you restrict the images of
drummers and delinquents to such stereotypes?

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.920
Plus, what kinda place do you
think Saitama Prefecture is?!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.260
It's because Saitama still has a lot of untouched nature.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:07.890
Come on! Get out here!

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.560
It has a very diverse ecosystem.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.680
Do you think pompadours are an endangered species?!

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.480
In manga and anime especially,

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.190
appearance and personality tend to match.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.150
For instance, red hair means you're passionate.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.320
Blue hair means you're calm and collected...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.490
Well... I guess those are commonly seen.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.410
And white hair means you're an old person.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.700
That's entirely normal!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.200
That's true, yeah.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.910
And green hair means you're unpopular.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.540
Please don't say things that'll
make us more enemies for no reason!

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.670
And black hair means you're pure.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.960
She just casually played up her own appeal!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.380
And green hair means you're unpopular.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.300
Don't repeat it!

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.930
When I think of "green,"

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:51.310
I think of how green-skinned characters
often produce eggs from their mouths.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.100
H-Have you seen someone
other than the "King" do that?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:01.070
Years ago, I practiced doing it with
hardboiled eggs, and my mother scolded me.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.690
What were you hoping to accomplish?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.740
Yellow is usually associated
with a love of curry, right?

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.030
What a healthy eater!

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.120
That's right!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.540
Red is the leader, Blue is the cool one,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.250
Pink gets fawned over because she's the only girl...

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.960
Aren't you a bit behind the times with that image?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:18.830
And green...

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.630
produces eggs from his mouth.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.420
No, we can let that joke die now.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.050
The mysterious criminal type usually
wears a black body stocking!

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.130
That's just artistic license!

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.800
Now I see.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.010
I always wondered why,
after the culprit's been discovered,

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.810
he suddenly stops wearing his body stocking.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.520
You're not very good at reading manga, are you?

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.560
When I think of black, I also think...

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.520
of coffee...

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.520
Black cats...

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.530
Silhouettes?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.400
Black suits...

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:48.780
Clothes of mourning...

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.300
Black hair is... pure.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.300
You don't give up!

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.810
And what was with that lead-in?

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.810
But in Sakura's case,

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.940
maybe instead of changing your
personality to match your appearance,

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.650
you should change your appearance
to match your personality?

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:22.610
Hm.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:23.690
That's also an option!

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.190
I don't like that idea.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.570
I don't want to see Sakura-senpai with a punch perm.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.530
What are you trying to say about me?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.320
Slurp!

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.660
Changing your appearance to
match your personality, huh?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.080
I guess there's only one way I can go...

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.930
Why shoulderpads?!

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.560
Okay. Go for the fingernails.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.680
Yeah.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:03.940
Hey!

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.570
What is this?!

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.030
This is too scary even for a penalty!

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.410
Lafcadio.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:30.420
Today, the heir to Hagitsuki-ryuu
has appeared in our sacred dojo...

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.720
...along with her friends.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.180
Hey, I came for some training.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:41.940
Hey, Botan.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.310
Are your nails unusually sparkly today?

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:46.860
Oh, this?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.900
Our junior member did it for me.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.410
I-I think it's cute.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.200
So you really do think of her as a friend!

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.210
Botan.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:05.460
I can come at you with everything
I've got today, right?

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.460
Yes. Try to kill me.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.260
That technique!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.220
You know it, Karin?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.100
It's kinda scary-looking!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.430
Don't make such misleading reactions!

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:25.020
This technique infuses my shadow
with <i>Nen</i> so I can control it as I wish!

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.820
I guess the shadow disappears
when the main form is defeated.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:35.780
She just attacked without listening to
the explanation of his special move!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.080
And after she beat him, she even added
her own supplementary explanation!

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.330
Fighting you one at a time is a pain.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.410
Come at me all at once.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.670
Botan sure is strong, isn't she?

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:47.960
Yeah...

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.750
I'm Suzaku of the Four Heavenly Kings.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:54.380
Just so you know, I've known Botan
since we were four years old!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.390
Ah... I see.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.970
Is she trying to compete with me?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:05.020
When we were in middle school,
we even went shopping for clothes together.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:06.100
Wow...

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:12.190
And this is the shirt I bought
at Botan's recommendation.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.900
Well, that's certainly...

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.030
a unique choice of clothing.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:20.280
You don't have to try to spare my feelings.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.490
It's a weird shirt that makes no sense.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:25.910
But this is...

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.750
the clothing Botan chose for me.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.920
It's a precious treasure to me.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:43.560
She defeated them without even
showing a moment's weakness!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.430
That's way too harsh for a battle anime!

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.770
Um, this isn't a battle anime.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.690
F-For some reason,

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.530
I'm the only one who didn't
get a proper caption...

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.530
but if you're curious, my name is—

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:01.530
You put up <i>that </i>one?!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.200
Welcome!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.580
A table for six?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.830
Botan-senpai, I've heard the story.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.170
Here, open wide!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.090
What story?

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:15.920
You said that Sakura-senpai was
the first friend you ever made.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:16.760
Is it good?

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:17.550
Yes!

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.800
But you went clothes shopping
with Suzaku once too, right?

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:20.970
Want another bite?

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:21.760
Yes!

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:21.890
Oh, that's right.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.260
Okay, open wide.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.010
Oh, that's right.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:25.600
I didn't understand why

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.140
she wanted to go shopping with me,
even though we were enemies.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:28.730
Ready for another bite?
she wanted to go shopping with me,
even though we were enemies.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.650
So I picked the weirdest piece of clothing
I'd seen all day and pushed her to buy it.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.600
Yes!

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.520
So I picked the weirdest piece of clothing
I'd seen all day and pushed her to buy it.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.030
We beg your indulgence in this matter.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:02.050
One, two, three, four, five, six...

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:03.850
No matter how many times she counted,

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.760
even though there should be one extra,

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.430
they were all faces she recognized...

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.440
She couldn't tell who the extra person was!

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.940
That's a pretty creepy story.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.190
But that's the hundredth story.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:20.860
After each of the "Hundred Ghost
Stories," we put out one candle.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.360
And this is the last one...

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:26.620
Wh-What will happen when we
put out the final candle?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.160
When I put out the hundredth candle...

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.080
animating the show becomes a lot easier!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:47.470
It's almost time to change uniforms.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.770
We didn't get much use out of the summer ones.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.600
Well, the fabric may actually be thin,

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.560
but when drawing them, the only
difference is whether the arms are visible.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.020
That's right.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:01.820
Even without relying on sex appeal,
it's enough that Karin is so cute.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.660
Well, be that as it may,

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.580
our club has five members now.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:11.410
This year, we can participate in the
club relay at the Athletics Festival!

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:12.870
Really?

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.460
Even though we're not an official club.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:18.340
What? No one told me we weren't official!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.170
If you sign up for the relay,

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:23.050
you can participate as just a group of friends.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.720
Oh, I see...

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:26.640
Then, I'll run anchor.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.470
What?!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.930
I'm the president! I should be the anchor!

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.890
Fine, but in that case...

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:35.690
There's a chance I might break someone's wrist.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.900
Please be the anchor!

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:44.910
Fanservice shot!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.620
And one more!

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.120
For the headband fetishists, too!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.080
Since my summer uniform didn't get much use,

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.160
I tried making up for it with my gym clothes!

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.880
Now, let's get out on that field
and practice some handoffs!

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.380
Well, we came out to the field...

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.170
but a sports club is already using it.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.300
It's okay!

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:09.510
This field belongs to everyone, so I'll
negotiate with them to let us use it!

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:17.060
But would they really give it up
in the middle of club practice?

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.520
Looks like it's not going well.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.570
Wow, she's totally flipping out!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.650
I ended up challenging them to a soccer match.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.070
How much did you complicate things?!

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:31.280
In 30 minutes, we'll have a match with the Soccer Club.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:34.870
If we win, they'll let us use
half the field however we want.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.460
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.630
All else aside, challenging the Soccer Club to soccer is...

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.210
Why did you decide to play them on their own turf?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.090
We're only five girls, remember?

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.890
Hey, it looks like she's only just realizing that now.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:52.220
Let's make a miracle happen
using the power of friendship.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.770
If that was all it took,
there'd be no need for training arcs!

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.890
I-If we don't have enough people,

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.230
can't we just run twice as hard to make up for it?

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:03.360
Do you run a sweatshop or something?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.400
Even if we do twice the work, we're still a player short.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.610
I just want to play soccer with you guys...

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.240
You can run ten times as hard by yourself.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:13.830
Now, now.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.870
If we win, they'll let us use the field, after all.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:20.830
Ah... but what happens if we lose?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:25.260
I offered Karin to them as their manager.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.880
Oh, as a manager?

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.270
Doumyouji!

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.520
Meet me on the roof!

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.900
That's a major overreaction!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:40.730
It's fine!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.810
We just have to win, right?

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.900
And so it seems

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.490
we've challenged them to a
battle we can't afford to lose.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.660
But how well do you guys actually
know the rules of soccer?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.700
Karin, why don't you tell
me everything you know?

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.460
Let's see...

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.630
you can't use your hands...

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.790
you kick the ball with your feet...

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:07.420
and you score points by getting
it in your opponent's goal.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:11.180
Also, if you slide in from behind, you get a card!

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:13.180
You jumped ahead to that?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.850
And if you get something called a
"hat trick," you get three points!

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.680
You've got the order backwards!

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.940
Okay then, Natsuki, can you
correctly explain the offside rule?

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:27.280
Offside is some kind of rule they have
in place to prevent ambushes, right?

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.280
Here goes!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:28.940
All right!

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:30.200
Aw, man!

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.240
What are the specific conditions for it?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.780
When is the ruling called?

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:37.040
How would you utilize an offside trap?

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.540
Um, I don't know that much about it...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.840
Plus, soccer is a game played
between two teams of eleven.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.250
Heavy... heavy...

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.090
I'm really sorry!

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.630
My arms are gonna fall off!

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:51.930
Then, let them fall off.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.760
I seriously can't feel my fingertips!

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:54.930
I think they're gonna tear off!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.180
That's not a problem. You don't
use your hands in soccer, anyway.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.350
B-But...

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.270
If you drop those buckets,
I'll feed you pickled grasshoppers.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:04.230
You're treating a Nagano Prefecture
staple food like a penalty?

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.780
It's fine. You don't have to
add any tedious disclaimers.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:11.650
Grasshoppers aren't a staple food.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.570
Hello, members of the Going Home Club.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:17.240
I'm the captain, Nakata.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:22.620
We are very grateful to you for
bringing us a female manager today.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.630
Karin's only a first-year,

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.290
but I've heard she's popular with the boys.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.210
Oh, are you really?

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.590
Have a lot of guys confessed to you?

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.130
Oh no, nothing like that.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.840
Oh, but Karin really is popular!

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.220
Like, not too long ago...

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.260
Could you not jump into girl talk so suddenly?

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.520
Wait a minute.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.270
This is the first I've heard about this.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.770
Who are these insects who have
been approaching Karin?

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.650
I won't allow any man weaker than me near her.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.690
I'll make sure they follow the proper procedures.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.530
Hey, Nakata!

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.900
Thanks to you, this has gotten way out of hand!

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:56.700
You're the one who started this
in the first place, President!

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.120
Well, say what you like.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.700
As long as Karin becomes our manager.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.910
Isn't it a bit early to be acting like you've won?

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:08.210
It's all five of us together that
make the Going Home Club what it is.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:11.670
We're indispensable friends
who all play leading roles.

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:14.840
We won't give up even one of our members!

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.720
Now she's posturing even though
this is all her own fault.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.180
Are you the Karin who's
becoming our manager?

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.430
Well, it's not set in stone yet...

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.560
It effectively is, though.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:29.230
Guys, don't get too overconfident.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:35.030
Don't forget that I could kill every one
of you in a single frame if I wanted to.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.320
A f-frame?

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:39.280
Why is she measuring increments of
time with fighting game terminology?

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.870
Hey, it's time to start!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.200
Take your positions!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.160
Yes, Captain!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:48.790
The match between the Soccer Club and
the Going Home Club will now begin!

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.660
What... kind of shot was that?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.700
That wasn't a shot.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:25.750
It was a pass.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:26.960
Zero points!

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.370
What kind of drive pass were you going for?

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.670
Hey, we'll resume the game with
a goal kick from your side!

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:35.340
No... it's okay. We forfeit.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.550
Please, use this half of the field.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.800
We can't use the goal over here, anyway...

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.060
And most of our club members wet themselves...

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.680
I wet myself, too.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.310
Sakura!

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.310
There, there.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.150
Didn't I tell you, Karin?

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:54.650
When hearts that protect and
hearts that believe overlap,

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:56.780
they won't lose to anyone.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:18:59.950
You've never told me that before,

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.410
but I'm still glad!

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.910
It's me.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.660
We ended the match safely.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.830
Recover the sniper, if you would.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:12.290
I'm better off not asking.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:23.140
Would the students participating in the club relay

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.510
please gather at the designated location.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.560
Ready...

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:31.310
Do your best, Sakura!

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:36.980
Go!

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.610
Do your best!

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.950
Sakura!

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.270
We did it! First place!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.810
This is what happens when the
five of us combine our powers!

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:15.230
And I was rooting for you as hard as I could!

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:15.980
Huh?

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:17.650
You were rooting for us?

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.780
There are five runners in a relay race,
and five members of the Going Home Club.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:24.360
And Karin was...

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.160
I was cheering for you the whole time.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.090
One...

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:39.750
two...

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.380
three...

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:42.880
four...

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:44.590
five?

00:22:45.880 --> 00:22:48.510
The chondrocladia lyra that
lives on the ocean floor is...

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:51.430
Um... how should I put it...

00:22:51.590 --> 00:22:53.180
What is it, exactly?

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:55.060
It's weird that this thing's a carnivore!

00:22:58.100 --> 00:22:59.270
And two more!
